-- title:
--   Primorial certificate data, block 19 of 75
-- statement:
--   Certificate data, block 19 of 75, for the primorial bound $\prod_{p\le n}p\cdot 25^n<68^n$ on $16\,000\,000<n\le 32\,000\,000$.
--
--   The block is a list of 35 records of the structure `Seg` from the definition `ThetaCertCore`. Together they cover the integers in $[16\,146\,435,\,16\,433\,155)$ in consecutive segments of length $2W=8\,192$. A record with fields $lo, hi, L, W, lo', hi'$ encodes the claim
--
--   $$
--   lo\le Q\,\theta(L-1)\le hi\ \Longrightarrow\ lo'\le Q\,\theta(L+2W-1)\le hi',
--   $$
--
--   where $\theta(x)=\sum_{p\le x}\log p$ is the Chebyshev function, the sum running over primes, and $Q=2^{64}$.
--
--   The records were produced by a program and are not trusted. The problem `PrimorialCert.block_19` states that every record passes the kernel-evaluated checker `Seg.bok`, that consecutive records connect, and that each record reaching past $16\,000\,001$ satisfies the inequality needed for the bound. The 75 blocks together form one chain from $L=3$ to $32\,006\,147$.
--
--   **Formalization Note** The field `ws` of every record is the empty list. The data are plain natural-number literals, so the definition needs nothing beyond `ThetaCertCore`.
-- source:
